          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of a
            %strong relative category
            is an extremely weak version of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKan1980Localizations"} Dwyer &amp; Kan 1980
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            (see there for more). A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on relative categories was constructed by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BarwickKan12"} Barwick &amp; Kan 2012
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            More generally, the notion of relative category captures the idea of having a distinguished
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
            of morphisms that should be preserved by functors. Relative categories are occasionally used for this purpose, unrelated to any higher categorical purpose.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#basic Basic
          %p
            A
            %strong relative category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi und
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi weq
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (und C, weq C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi und
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} und C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi weq
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} weq C
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi weq
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} weq C
            is said to be a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong relative functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi und
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi und
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon und C \to und D
            that preserves weak equivalences in the obvious sense.
          %p
            The
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of a relative category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the ordinary category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho C
            obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi und
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} und C
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} freely inverting
            the weak equivalences in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#refinements Refinements
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong semi-saturated relative category
                is a relative category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                such that every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi und
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} und C
                is a weak equivalence in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
                is a semi-saturated relative category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi weq
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} weq C
                has the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three+property"} two-out-of-three property
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
                is a relative category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi weq
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} weq C
                has the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-six+property"} two-out-of-six property
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                a category with weak equivalences.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong saturated homotopical category
                is a relative category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                such that a morphism is a weak equivalence
                %em if and only if
                it is invertible in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho C
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The semi-saturation condition is precisely the condition on the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi weq
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi und
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} weq C \to und C
              ensuring it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} monomorphism
              in the (2,1)-category of 1-categories.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Any ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            gives rise to three relative categories in a functorial way:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong minimal relative category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi min
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} min C
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identities
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong minimal homotopical category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi min
                          %mo +
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} min^+ C
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphisms
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong maximal homotopical category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi max
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} max C
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#categories_of_relative_categories Categories of relative categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi RelCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{RelCat}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            relative categories and relative functors. It is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally finitely presentable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponential object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C, D]_h
            as the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong relative functor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi RelCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{RelCat}
            is, in particular, a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"}> strict
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi SsRelCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{SsRelCat}
            be the full subcategory of semi-saturated relative categories. The inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi SsRelCat
                  %mo ↪
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi RelCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{SsRelCat} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{RelCat}
            has a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint"} adjoint
            that preserves finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi SsRelCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{SsRelCat}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ideal"} exponential ideal
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi RelCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{RelCat}
          %p
            There are then the following strings of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi min
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi und
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi max
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi weq
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi RelCat
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} min \dashv und \dashv max \dashv weq : \mathbf{RelCat} \to \mathbf{Cat}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi min
                    %mo +
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi RelCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho \dashv min^+ : \mathbf{Cat} \to \mathbf{RelCat}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi min
                    %mo +
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi und
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi max
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi weq
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi SsRelCat
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho \dashv min^+ \dashv und \dashv max \dashv weq : \mathbf{SsRelCat} \to \mathbf{Cat}
          %p
            Moreover, because
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi min
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} min^+
            embeds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Cat}
            as a reflective exponential ideal in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi SsRelCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{SsRelCat}
            and in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi RelCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{RelCat}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi SsRelCat
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho : \mathbf{SsRelCat} \to \mathbf{Cat}
            preserves finite products.
          %h3#AsEnrichedCategories As enriched categories
          %p
            The application of relative categories as expressing the idea of having a subcategory of distinguished morphisms can be neatly packaged into viewing relative categories as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            over the category of sets with distinguished subsets. An equivalent formulation is that of an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-category"} M-category
            (see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-category"} F-category
            for a
            = succeed "-theoretic" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PairSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PairSet
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            whose objects are pairs of small sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, A)
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, A) \to (Y, B)
            are functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(A) \subseteq B
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RelCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RelCat
              is isomorphic to the category of small
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PairSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PairSet
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              With minimal rephrasing, a small
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PairSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PairSet
            %ul
              %li
                A small set of objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                For objects
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,Y)
                with a subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(X,Y)
              %li
                For objects
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y,Z
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(Y,Z) \times C(X,Y) \to C(X,Z)
                that restricts to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(Y,Z) \times W(X,Y) \to W(X,Z)
              %li
                For objects
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_X \in W(X,X)
            %p
              that is subject to identity and associativity relations. It’s immediate that this is exactly the same data as a relative category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
          %h3#model_structures Model structures
          %p
            A relative category can be equipped with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+model+structure"} weak model structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semimodel+structure"} semimodel structure
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure"} model structure
          %p
            These structures do not change the underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
          %h3#presentation_of_categories
            Presentation of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The theory of relative categories presents a theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            in the following sense:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p There exists an adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi ξ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ξ
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi RelCat
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi ssSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_\xi \dashv N_\xi : \mathbf{RelCat} \to \mathbf{ssSet}
            %p
              such that every left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              on the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi ssSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{ssSet}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
              induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly-generated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi RelCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{RelCat}
              making the adjunction a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi RelCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{RelCat}
              that is Quillen equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for complete Segal spaces
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi ssSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{ssSet}
          %p
            This is discussed in further detail at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+categories+with+weak+equivalences"} model structure on categories with weak equivalences
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+relative+category"} monoidal relative category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-category"} F-category
            %li
              %p
