            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/marked+simplicial+set"} marked simplicial set
          %h2#References References
          %p The terminology “relative categories” is due to
          %ul
            %li#BarwickKan12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "." do
                %em Relative categories: Another model for the homotopy theory of homotopy theories
              %strong 23
              (2012) 42-68 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.1691"}> arXiv:1011.1691
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indag.2011.10.002"} doi:10.1016/j.indag.2011.10.002
          %p while the basic idea goes back, at least, to:
          %ul
            %li#DwyerKan1980Localizations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simplicial localizations of categories
              %strong 17
              (1980) 267-284. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049%2880%2990049-3"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(80)90049-3
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            (cf. the
            %a{:href => "category+with+weak+equivalences#References"} references
            at “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"}> category with weak equivalences
            ”).
